01:18:44.990 --> 01:18:50.500
&gt;&gt; So the last piece of our
portfolio, specific solutions to

01:18:50.500 --> 01:18:55.130
enable digital transformation
in specific industries. One of

01:18:55.820 --> 01:19:01.400
our important assets at Google
is Geo. And to show you how

01:19:01.490 --> 01:19:06.700
companies and Enterprises are
using Geo to transform their

01:19:06.700 --> 01:19:11.000
business, please welcome Jen
Fitzpatrick, senior Vice

01:19:11.000 --> 01:19:18.200
President of Geo at Google.
[Applause]

01:19:24.940 --> 01:19:28.440
&gt;&gt; Good morning, everybody. I'm
 happy to be here to share with

01:19:28.440 --> 01:19:32.880
you today what we've been up to
in our Geo work at Google. For

01:19:32.880 --> 01:19:36.470
more than a decade now, we've
been mapping the world and

01:19:36.480 --> 01:19:39.680
translating that knowledge and
understanding into meaningful

01:19:39.680 --> 01:19:44.770
experiences for our users. We
started many years ago by

01:19:44.770 --> 01:19:48.480
mapping roads so we could help
people reliably get from point A

01:19:48.490 --> 01:19:52.950
to point B. But over time, what
 we've seen is our users showing

01:19:52.950 --> 01:19:55.370
an appetite for more and more
types of knowledge and

01:19:55.370 --> 01:19:59.300
understanding about the real
world. They asked us more and

01:19:59.300 --> 01:20:03.020
more complex questions, and they
 fully expected maps to be able

01:20:03.020 --> 01:20:06.660
to provide helpful answers or
experiences in new types of

01:20:06.660 --> 01:20:10.430
contexts. So we sought off to
deepen our understanding of the

01:20:10.430 --> 01:20:14.650
world, to bring new types of
knowledge and understanding to

01:20:14.650 --> 01:20:20.070
the map as well as more dynamic
and realtime content. The real

01:20:20.070 --> 01:20:23.500
world changes fast, and keeping
up with the pace of that change

01:20:23.630 --> 01:20:27.750
can be a challenge. But in
recent years, advances in

01:20:27.750 --> 01:20:31.070
technology have helped us get
smarter about the way that we

01:20:31.070 --> 01:20:36.320
build maps. Using the power of
Machine Learning and what we

01:20:36.320 --> 01:20:39.270
know about the world through
things like imagery and user

01:20:39.270 --> 01:20:42.620
contributed content, we're able
to keep Google Maps fresh,

01:20:42.970 --> 01:20:46.930
accurate and realtime for more
than a billion users all around

01:20:46.930 --> 01:20:51.980
the world. Let's take a quick
look at how we do that. We use

01:20:51.980 --> 01:20:54.800
Machine Learning algorithms to
look for changes in satellite

01:20:54.800 --> 01:20:58.140
imagery which allows us to
automatically detect new roads.

01:20:59.360 --> 01:21:02.280
Based on this approach, over the
 last nine months, we have added

01:21:02.290 --> 01:21:05.050
half a million kilometers of
new roads in more than 20

01:21:05.060 --> 01:21:09.450
countries. With a similar
technique, we can automatically

01:21:09.450 --> 01:21:12.160
detect and draw building
outlines, which has allowed us

01:21:12.170 --> 01:21:14.900
to more than double the total
number of buildings on the map

01:21:15.250 --> 01:21:19.670
around the world in less than a
year. We continue to push the

01:21:19.670 --> 01:21:22.470
bounds of what it means to map
the world and to have an

01:21:22.470 --> 01:21:27.580
incredibly rich and up to date
data model.
Now, what does this

01:21:27.580 --> 01:21:31.250
have to do with all of you?
Google maps platform is the

01:21:31.250 --> 01:21:33.760
means by which we give our
enterprise customers access to

01:21:33.760 --> 01:21:37.430
the same rich and complex real
world information that we use to

01:21:37.430 --> 01:21:41.880
power our consumer products.
This has long been an area of

01:21:41.880 --> 01:21:45.130
focus for us. In fact, our
original maps APIs are well over

01:21:45.130 --> 01:21:48.360
ten years old. What we see
happening today is a real

01:21:48.360 --> 01:21:52.230
acceleration in businesses
finding new ways to use location

01:21:52.410 --> 01:21:55.270
and real world insights to
transform their customer

01:21:55.270 --> 01:21:59.180
experiences as well as how they
operate.
Let me share a few

01:21:59.180 --> 01:22:03.370
examples. Transportation has
always been an obvious area of

01:22:03.370 --> 01:22:05.720
focus for us given our core
emphasis on helping people

01:22:05.720 --> 01:22:09.290
navigate the world. And as the
transportation industry

01:22:09.290 --> 01:22:12.630
continues to transform, we're
partnering with many different

01:22:12.630 --> 01:22:18.180
players, from automakers to ride
 sharing to public transit. In

01:22:18.180 --> 01:22:21.050
the automotive space, we've
partnered with automakers for

01:22:21.140 --> 01:22:25.750
years to bring information from
Google maps into cars, but in

01:22:25.750 --> 01:22:28.490
recent years, we've begun going
deeper, partnering with auto

01:22:28.490 --> 01:22:32.710
companies like Volvo and
Mistusibhi to bring a fully

01:22:32.710 --> 01:22:36.760
embedded voice driven, auto
tailored version of Google maps

01:22:36.760 --> 01:22:39.750
and the Google assistant to the
car, and we're excited to see

01:22:39.750 --> 01:22:42.720
the first cars with this new
experience hit the streets next

01:22:42.720 --> 01:22:47.240
year.
But really, this is just
the start. Cars are quickly

01:22:47.240 --> 01:22:50.530
becoming more connected and
gathering larger and larger

01:22:50.530 --> 01:22:54.220
volumes of sensor data. So
whether it's making sense of

01:22:54.790 --> 01:22:58.700
telemetry data from cars or
spotting part performance trends

01:22:58.980 --> 01:23:02.120
or helping manage in car
machine learning and compute, we

01:23:02.120 --> 01:23:07.176
see many ways that we can
partner together.
Ride sharing

01:23:07.200 --> 01:23:10.020
is another industry that we
partner closely with. Today we

01:23:10.020 --> 01:23:12.860
power more than 800 million
routes each day for customers

01:23:12.860 --> 01:23:19.410
like Ola, DD, Go Jack, Lyft,
MyTaxi, and more. Beyond just

01:23:19.410 --> 01:23:22.640
navigation, though, we're
helping to provide insights that

01:23:22.640 --> 01:23:25.300
can drive realtime decisions
and optimizations for their

01:23:25.300 --> 01:23:29.330
vehicle fleets so operations get
 more efficient and riders and

01:23:29.330 --> 01:23:32.830
drivers can have a great
experience. We're excited to

01:23:32.830 --> 01:23:35.390
keep innovating with our
partners to unlock even more

01:23:35.390 --> 01:23:38.460
benefits to the transportation
industry, as well as for cities

01:23:38.460 --> 01:23:43.450
and public transit agencies all
around the world.
The

01:23:43.450 --> 01:23:47.020
information that we know about
places, businesses on the map,

01:23:47.020 --> 01:23:49.990
and points of interest all
around the world also bring

01:23:50.000 --> 01:23:53.380
great opportunity for
enterprises of many types. Let

01:23:53.380 --> 01:23:56.860
me share a few more examples.
Last year we introduced a

01:23:56.860 --> 01:24:00.586
tailored solution for the gaming
 industry, letting game studios

01:24:00.610 --> 01:24:04.700
use the power of Google maps to
build real world games, creating

01:24:04.710 --> 01:24:08.890
virtual game worlds based on
real life locations or creating

01:24:08.900 --> 01:24:11.780
game play in the real world
based on the Maps' knowledge of

01:24:11.870 --> 01:24:16.080
where the best spots to play
are.
The game studio Mixi was

01:24:16.080 --> 01:24:19.410
an early customer and partner
for us here. And when they added

01:24:19.410 --> 01:24:22.020
a real world experience to
their already successful game

01:24:22.030 --> 01:24:26.080
Monster Strike, they saw a 30%
increase in daily sessions per

01:24:26.080 --> 01:24:31.160
user. And this experience isn't
unique to gaming. As the world

01:24:31.160 --> 01:24:34.830
has gone mobile, location based
capabilities are repeatedly

01:24:34.830 --> 01:24:38.010
transforming customer
experiences across a wide range

01:24:38.010 --> 01:24:42.270
of industries.
The travel
industry is another area where

01:24:42.270 --> 01:24:45.050
knowledge of real world places
is absolutely critical to

01:24:45.050 --> 01:24:48.810
success. And so we're working
with travel booking sites to add

01:24:48.810 --> 01:24:51.100
our deep understanding of
places directly into their

01:24:51.110 --> 01:24:55.790
customer experiences. Servicing
the right information about what

01:24:55.790 --> 01:24:59.340
places are nearby when someone
is trying to make a decision can

01:24:59.340 --> 01:25:03.270
help drive conversions and turn
 casual explorers into real

01:25:03.270 --> 01:25:07.830
customers. These are just a few
of the innovative ways we see

01:25:07.830 --> 01:25:10.350
our customers taking advantage
of the Google maps platform.

01:25:11.470 --> 01:25:14.070
Now, many of my examples today
have been about enterprises

01:25:14.080 --> 01:25:16.740
using Google Maps platform to
provide better experiences for

01:25:16.740 --> 01:25:19.970
their customers, but we're also
working with companies around

01:25:19.970 --> 01:25:22.400
the globe to provide real world
insights that help drive

01:25:22.410 --> 01:25:27.470
operational efficiency. From
retail to insurance to finance

01:25:27.470 --> 01:25:30.950
and more, we're helping with
things like where to best target

01:25:30.970 --> 01:25:33.810
your promotional spend, where
to best locate your next

01:25:33.810 --> 01:25:38.300
storefront, and many, many more
things beyond. So no matter what

01:25:38.300 --> 01:25:41.980
industry you're in, location
based data and insights can have

01:25:41.980 --> 01:25:44.980
a powerful impact on your
business, and today more so than

01:25:44.980 --> 01:25:48.490
ever. We encourage you to think
 about how you can use the power

01:25:48.500 --> 01:25:51.880
of location to transform your
business. And with that, I'll

01:25:51.880 --> 01:25:56.410
turn it back to Thomas.
[Applause]

01:26:00.680 --> 01:26:06.530
&gt;&gt; So we at Google are using
our cloud to bring the best of

01:26:06.550 --> 01:26:11.100
all of Google's technologies to
enterprises. And one of the

01:26:11.110 --> 01:26:15.480
industries that we've had a long
 history of working with is

01:26:15.480 --> 01:26:22.400
health care. Our mission is to
help organize different kinds of

01:26:22.400 --> 01:26:26.920
information that health care
providers need, like electronic

01:26:26.930 --> 01:26:31.980
medical record information,
genomic data information,

01:26:33.460 --> 01:26:38.450
clinical trials information to
